From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: memory: mediatek: add the MT6897 video coprocessor port

The video coprocessor (VCP) of the MT6897 reaches the MDP IOMMU without an
SMI larb. The vendor numbers such masters as larb43, which does not fit the
five bits the port ID has for a larb. No larb of this SoC is number 31, so
use that.
---
 include/dt-bindings/memory/mediatek,mt6897-memory-port.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/dt-bindings/memory/mediatek,mt6897-memory-port.h b/include/dt-bindings/memory/mediatek,mt6897-memory-port.h
index 31902bdbb..9a292506c 100644
--- a/include/dt-bindings/memory/mediatek,mt6897-memory-port.h
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/memory/mediatek,mt6897-memory-port.h
@@ -38,4 +38,10 @@
 #define M4U_PORT_L5_HW_VDEC_LAT0_UFO_ENC_EXT	MTK_M4U_ID(5, 7)
 #define M4U_PORT_L5_HW_VDEC_LAT0_UFO_ENC_C_EXT	MTK_M4U_ID(5, 8)
 
+/*
+ * larb31 is not a larb. It stands for the masters that reach the MDP IOMMU
+ * without one. The vendor counts them as larb43, which does not fit the ID.
+ */
+#define M4U_PORT_L31_VIDEO_UP			MTK_M4U_ID(31, 0)
+
 #endif
